@startuml 10-visitor-privacy
skinparam backgroundColor #F7F8FA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Aptos
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam ArrowColor #566173
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #168B80
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #E6F4F1
skinparam ActorBorderColor #667085
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #F3F4F6
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #4969C5
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #EAF0FF

actor "Visitor" as visitor
participant "Atlas mobile app" as app
participant "Privacy boundary" as privacy
database "Event store\nshort-lived / minimised" as store
participant "Aggregation jobs" as agg
participant "B2B dashboard" as dashboard

visitor -> app : Uses map / navigation
app -> app : Check analytics consent\nand applicable policy

alt analytics not allowed
  app -> app : Do not emit movement analytics
else analytics allowed
  app -> privacy : Position sample + session context
  privacy -> privacy : Remove direct identity\nrotate pseudonymous session ID
  privacy -> store : Anonymous location event\nvenue + map version + timestamp
  store -> agg : Batch / stream event
  agg -> agg : Aggregate by time, floor, zone\napply minimum cohort thresholds
  agg -> dashboard : Dwell, flow, density, footfall\nwith quality / confidence
end

note over privacy, dashboard
Operator view is about populations and operations.
It does not require visitor names, contact details,
or an individual movement trail.
end note

note bottom
Consent, retention, access control, deletion and legal basis are product requirements,
not merely implementation details. Raw exports remain restricted and auditable.
end note
@enduml
